<!-- 
| Feature/Gaps           | Status    | Technical Observation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| **Register Map**       | **FULL**  | Populated based on `pwm_reg.h`. The BL808 PWM controller consists of 2 independent groups (Multi-Channel blocks), each with 4 channels.                                                                                                                                               |
| **Architecture**       | **Cluster**| Implemented using a `<cluster>` with `dim=2` and `dimIncrement=0x40` to represent Group 0 (0x00) and Group 1 (0x40).                                                                                                                                                                 |
| **Thresholds**         | **Array**  | Threshold registers (`THRE%s`) are implemented as an array of 4 within each group cluster, covering CH0-CH3.                                                                                                                                                                          |
| **Interrupts**         | **Granular**| Maps separate Low (L) and High (H) threshold interrupts for every channel, plus Period, Break, and Repeat events.                                                                                                                                                                     |
| **Advanced PWM**       | **FULL**  | Includes Dead-Time Generators (DTG), Software/External Break logic, and the PWM-to-ADC hardware trigger source selection (`pwm_adc_trg_src`).                                                                                                                                         |
| **Reset Values**       | Added     | Reset values for all fields integrated from the `struct pwm_channel_reg` bitfield annotations (e.g., `pwm_stop_mode` default 1, `pwm_chX_nsi` default 1).                                                                                                                              |
| **Base Address**       | Explicit | 0x2000A400.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
-->
